# Extra mysqld command-line flags for the shared MySQL test container
# (SharedDbContainerService). One token per line; blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored.
#
# Why these are safe HERE (and would NOT be safe in production): this
# container is disposable and is torn down at the end of every test run,
# so there is no need for crash durability, replication, or monitoring.
#
# Measured effect (apache/gravitino#13553, 8vCPU/31GB gcp-arc-runners-large
# class, -PcoreDatabaseForks=2), core:coreMySQLTest wall clock:
#   26m25s  per-fork containers (old design)
#   27m53s  shared container, untuned
#   22m15s  shared container, first 4 flags below only
#    7m04s  shared container, all flags below + tmpfs data dir
# All runs: 520 tests, 0 failures, 0 deadlocks / lock-wait timeouts.
# core:coreH2Test is unchanged across all runs (1m27s -> 1m21s), the control
# confirming the speedup is database I/O and not the host.
--innodb-flush-log-at-trx-commit=0
--sync-binlog=0
--innodb-buffer-pool-size=2G
--innodb-log-buffer-size=64M
--skip-log-bin
--innodb-doublewrite=0
--performance-schema=OFF
